# Targets chezmoi should DELETE from a machine, not just stop managing.
#
# Deleting a file from the source state only makes chezmoi forget about it —
# the copy already on disk stays there forever, still on PATH, still runnable.
# For a retired command that is worse than useless: it keeps working just well
# enough to be trusted, long after the thing it talks to has moved.
#
# Entries here are applied on every `chezmoi apply`, so they are safe to leave
# in place, and worth leaving in place until every machine has certainly run
# one.

# browser-vpn: an `ssh -D` SOCKS5 proxy to claude-server, replaced by the
# routed path (10.47.0.0/16 via the server) plus split DNS on port 5300.
# Removed 2026-08-17. See docs/client-work-setup.md.
.local/bin/browser-vpn

# claude-attach-herdr: existed only for the herdr-vs-tmux comparison. herdr won
# and claude-attach itself is now the herdr client, with --tmux as the escape
# hatch, so this one is a second name for the same thing.
# Removed 2026-08-19. See docs/server-setup.md.
.local/bin/claude-attach-herdr
